description: Python backend, TypeScript frontend, OpenAPI-generated types
alwaysApply: true
---

# Stack

- Backend: Python. Owns the chat API, local LLM, and TTS.
- Frontend: TypeScript. UI only; talks to the Python API.
- Contracts: OpenAPI (or equivalent schema) on the backend generates TypeScript request/response types for the frontend.

Don’t

- Run a TypeScript backend (or a second API in Node) just to share types.
- Duplicate models by hand on both sides when generation exists.
- Move LLM or TTS into the browser or a cloud host.
